#hash((content-digest . "1ff005b1341d388a5fd896460eb13f46951b0a6d43741f67e06c9a29029a1b09") (content-digest-command . "git diff --binary origin/main...HEAD -- . (excluding gsd-wave-evidence/reviews/validation) | sha256sum") (non-blocking-findings . ("tests/test-gsd-github-port.rkt uses a silent-success runner (exit 0 with no per-check output line); count taken from the artifact census (19 checks) rather than the runner output" "mutation evidence is manual micro-mutations (M1, M2) rather than the automated mutation pilot, recorded per the adequacy contract")) (report . "APPROVED. W5 delivers semantic-redundancy detection and consolidation governance without weakening detection power. scripts/run-tests/redundancy-candidates.rkt pairs tests from the W0 census by @covers identity, fixture-builder reuse, and stimulus-sequence overlap, and emits candidate groups with evidence links; tests/test-redundancy-candidates.rkt (16 checks, red-first) asserts the pairing rules, evidence-link emission, and preference-order decisions. Detection found exactly one candidate family G1 (tests/test-gsd-delivery-verifier.rkt 24 checks + tests/test-gsd-github-port.rkt 19 checks, paired by family adjacency across the delivery-verification/github-port seam); the static detector reports distinct @covers keys, no shared fixture, and non-shared stimulus (fake delivery-verification child process vs fake github adapter), so G1 resolves to keep-both at preference-order step 3 — no merge, no deletion, counts before=43 after=43. Adequacy artifact (test-consolidation-adequacy/1) carries before/after counts, G1 behavior mapping, failure-history review (ANALYSIS-v1.00.04-W0-DELIVERY-VERIFIER-COMMITTED-FALSE-NEGATIVE.md), and manual micro-mutation evidence on extensions/gsd/delivery-verifier.rkt: M1 (branch-equality relaxation, previously killed) still killed; M2 (sync approval gate exit-code forgery, previously killed) still killed — no detection regression; M2-async is out of suite scope and no test was moved onto it. The prior attempt's failure (adequacy.json unreadable at verify time) is addressed: the artifact now exists on the delivery branch, parses, and mutation-pilot --check reports OK. Consolidation report TEST-CONSOLIDATION-v1.00.28.md is checksummed via SHA256SUMS (candidates.json, adequacy.json, report — all OK). Focused: redundancy-candidates 16/0/0, delivery-verifier 24/0/0, github-port exit 0, adequacy --check OK, checksums OK, metrics resynced (lint 23 passed, 2 non-blocking warnings). The previously failed delivery verification path (missing adequacy.json) is verified fixed.") (reviewed-sha . "3659491cf60f9479c491f59da516db10c491bc44") (reviewer . "orchestrator pre-merge evidence") (scope . "v1.00.28 W5 #9593 semantic redundancy and shared-stimulus consolidation") (timestamp . "2026-09-09T15:30:40Z") (verdict . "APPROVED"))
